  "name": "Transferrin Saturation",
  "code": "Transferrin",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Transferrin Saturation</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Normal Range (typically 30-60%)</div></td><td><div>Indicates normal iron saturation levels in transferrin</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Increased Levels</div></td><td><div>High transferrin saturation may suggest iron overload disorders such as hereditary hemochromatosis or secondary hemochromatosis. It can also be seen in certain chronic liver diseases or frequent blood transfusions. Further evaluation is necessary to determine the underlying cause.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Decreased Levels</div></td><td><div>Low transferrin saturation levels may indicate iron deficiency anemia or other conditions where there is insufficient iron available for binding to transferrin. It can also be seen in chronic inflammatory conditions or certain chronic diseases. Additional testing is required to identify the underlying cause.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
